(Seeded PRNG: a linear congruential generator. Deterministic per seed,
 which is what makes every finding reproducible from its seed alone.)

a number called rng_state is 12345.

To 'rng seed' with a number called s.
    Set rng_state to s.

To 'rng next'.
    Set rng_state to rng_state multiply 1103515245.
    Set rng_state to rng_state add 12345.
    Set rng_state to rng_state modulo 2147483648.
    Return a number, rng_state.

(A draw below nn, taken from the HIGH bits of the state - fuzzer defect
 13.

 The low bits of a power-of-two-modulus LCG are not random: bit 0 has
 period 2, so `r modulo nn` handed every caller a sequence whose parity
 alternated. Measured over 10 000 draws before this changed: `'rng
 below' of 2` gave 0,1,0,1,... - 5000 of each, longest run 1, lag-1
 autocorrelation -0.999 - and `of 10` never repeated a value either,
 longest run 1, because consecutive draws always disagreed in parity.
 Every coin flip in every leaf was perfectly anti-correlated with the
 one before it, and any helper spending a fixed number of draws per
 construct locked onto the alternation and stopped varying at all.

 Multiply-high instead of modulo: r is below 2^31, so `r multiply nn`
 divided by 2^31 is r's position below nn scaled by its HIGH bits, and
 the low bit no longer reaches the result at all. The same 10 000 draws
 after the change: below 2 gives longest run 12 and lag-1 -0.014, below
 3 longest run 9 and -0.006, below 10 longest run 4 and -0.004 - the
 runs are now what fair draws give, log2 10000 and log10 10000.
 tests/230_units.vox pins all three.

 nn is small everywhere it is called - the largest is 1000000 - so
 `r multiply nn` stays far below the 64-bit ceiling. nn of 0 still
 yields 0, as `r modulo 0` did: tests/230_units.vox pins that too,
 because the fuzzer's seed reproduction must not become a divide by
 zero.)

To 'rng below' with a number called nn.
    a number called r is 'rng next'.
    a number called 'the scaled draw' is r multiply nn.
    Return a number, 'the scaled draw' divide 2147483648.
